{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_011Ceu8RjSyjJKwvejsa35Li","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XWosRRP4uGxCGNuApkHSAw","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/bear/Documents/CoWork/bear-textbooks/books/anthropics/claude-code-101/03-hooks-skills-commands/cc-hook-enforcement/scratch/summary.md","content":"# Student summaries\n\n_Note: per project rules, only the teacher awards letter grades. Summaries below report raw scores and short observations only._\n\n## Ada\nAda scored 88 on quiz 1 and improved to 92 on quiz 2, showing an upward trajectory across the two assessments. Her project score of 90 is consistent with her quiz work, indicating that she applies the material at roughly the same level she demonstrates on shorter assessments. Attendance was perfect at 10/10, so participation was not a limiting factor. Overall: strong, consistent work with visible improvement between quizzes.\n\n## Boris\nBoris scored 72 on quiz 1 and 78 on quiz 2 — a meaningful gain that suggests the second unit clicked better than the first, or that his study approach adjusted. His project came in noticeably higher at 84, which points to stronger performance on applied, longer-form work than on timed quizzes. Attendance was 9/10, essentially full. Overall: solid mid-range work, trending upward, with applied work as his stronger mode.\n\n## Cai\nCai posted the top marks in the group: 95 on quiz 1, 90 on quiz 2, and 96 on the project, with perfect 10/10 attendance. Quiz 2 dipped slightly from quiz 1 but remained well above class-typical performance, and the project score suggests the material is well-consolidated. Overall: consistently excellent across every measured dimension.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":833,"cache_read_input_tokens":47983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_inp